+# Timer executes the statements through an interpreter over a DOCUMENTED
+# subset of Python:
+#   * 'pass'
+#   * assignment:            name = expr
+#   * tuple assignment:      a, b = b, a        (any arity)
+#   * expressions:          literals, names, tuples, and + - * / % // with
+#                           parentheses (including unary minus)
+# Values live in a dict; tuples are represented as Python lists.
+# Anything outside the subset fails closed with NotImplementedError: PITON
+# must never "time" code it did not actually run.
+#
+# NOTE: token text is built by character accumulation, never by a computed
+# slice (AGENTS2 T1: a computed slice returned from a function is a pointer).
